KG42.register("edges-9dccf0303f58aaf11a602ca3",{"id":"S-8d6c13f68cf0fd5e","source":"KG31-b9a1f3b2c60ed604","type":"links","target":"KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation"],"assertions":[{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::E::v141-c-R014-E002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R014","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R014-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R014-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-b9a1f3b2c60ed604","target":"KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. | MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. | MMR pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"602f77bf55626b9ece6809c129a52592f191296a2a993b02ee48bd1a5e4be0ef","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","source_definition":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","target_definition":"Submitted generation quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. Submitted demand quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. The coordinator calculates internal prices using the MMR pricing model. Scope: MMR pricing within one energy sharing region. The internal buying and selling prices are equal to the arithmetic mean of the retailer's export and retail prices. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation equals total demand. The internal selling price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal buying price is adjusted to cover the regional deficit imported at the retailer's retail price. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation is less than total demand. The internal buying price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal selling price is adjusted to incorporate surplus-export income for distribution among participants providing electricity through generation or EV discharging. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation exceeds total demand.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted generation quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["e_gen_bid_nt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A25-A27","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids of all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal price in different ways according to the relationship between total generation and demand in the energy sharing region. If the generation is equal to demand, the internal buying and selling price are equal, taking the average of the export and retail price:\n\np_t^{buy} = p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} = \\frac{(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})}{2}, \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| = \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A25)\n\nIf the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered. Therefore, in this situation, the internal selling price keeps the same as that in Formula (A25), but the buying price is modified:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A26)\n\nSimilarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging. The internal price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A27)\n\nFormulas (A25)-(A27) compose the pricing model in the coordinator agent under mid-market rate mechanism."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. | MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. | MMR pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R014-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}}],"assertion_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::E::v141-c-R014-E002"]});
